&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fqkz0gho09u5sxjf2s40d.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fqkz0gho09u5sxjf2s40d.png" alt="The orders page: a heading and three order cards, the middle one under the pointer." width="800" height="327"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The page has a breakpoint, a hover state and a dark theme. Each is just one more rule, so all three render on the server like the rest. You don't configure anything for this. The package's &lt;code&gt;react-server&lt;/code&gt; export condition gives a Server Component a build of Box that calls no hook and never touches the DOM. Importing it is the whole setup.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Look at the HTML response and you'll find two &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;style&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; elements in &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;head&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. React merges each &lt;code&gt;precedence&lt;/code&gt; group into one element and lists what it merged in &lt;code&gt;data-href&lt;/code&gt;. Every class in the markup has its rule in that response, so nothing waits for JavaScript to define it. The class names are hashes of their content, which is why the class the server wrote is exactly the class a client bundle would compute. Hydration has nothing to disagree about.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The order of the rules is not left to chance either. React hoists elements in the order it meets them, and rules are shared between Boxes, so element order alone could let &lt;code&gt;p&lt;/code&gt; override &lt;code&gt;px&lt;/code&gt;. Every rule therefore sits in a cascade layer, and the first style element declares the order of all layers once. Layer order beats source order.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What it costs, measured
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Talk of "zero runtime" is cheap, so here are numbers instead. The setup:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a Next.js 16.3.5 production build (&lt;code&gt;next start&lt;/code&gt;) with React 19.3, measured on a laptop;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a page of cards like the one above, each a &lt;code&gt;Flex&lt;/code&gt; with an &lt;code&gt;H2&lt;/code&gt;, a &lt;code&gt;P&lt;/code&gt; and a &lt;code&gt;Span&lt;/code&gt; inside, so four Boxes per card;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a baseline page with the same markup, styled by a plain CSS module.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Both pages render on every request.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Cards&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;HTML, gzipped (Box / CSS module)&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Server response, median of 40 (Box / CSS module)&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;100&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;11.2 KB / 4.4 KB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;15 ms / 10 ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1,000&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;33.6 KB / 24.7 KB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;79 ms / 35 ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The JavaScript the browser downloaded was &lt;strong&gt;byte for byte the same on both pages&lt;/strong&gt;: Next.js's own runtime, 172.9 KB gzipped. None of those chunks contained the styling engine. On a page with no client component, the engine never leaves the server.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Two costs show in the table, and both are real:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Rendering a Box takes time.&lt;/strong&gt; At 1,000 cards, the page with 4,000 Boxes took 44 ms longer to render than the one with plain class names, which is about 11 µs per Box. Boxes styled alike resolve through one cache lookup, so a long list of identical rows costs less than a page of all-different elements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The CSS travels in the HTML.&lt;/strong&gt; A CSS module is a file the browser caches once for the whole site, while these rules come with each response. Most of the gap at 100 cards is the base stylesheet: the reset and the layer order, about 24 KB before compression, sent with every page.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  What measuring this turned up
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The first run of this benchmark didn't look like the table above. The page with 1,000 cards weighed &lt;strong&gt;102 MB&lt;/strong&gt;. On screen everything was right: two style elements in &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;head&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, every class styled. The extra weight was in the RSC payload, the copy of the component tree that Next.js puts under the HTML for the client to pick up. React removes duplicate style elements from the page, but the payload carried every Box's elements in full, including the 24 KB base stylesheet, once per Box.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The fix is in the library: every Box now gets the &lt;em&gt;same&lt;/em&gt; element objects. React's serializer sends an object it has already sent as a short reference, so the base stylesheet now crosses the wire once. That turned 102 MB into the 1.3 MB of the table above, and it shipped in Box Kite 2.2.4. A regression check now measures it against a real Next.js build on every pull request, because no unit test could have seen it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Suspense streams the CSS with the markup
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Streaming is where collecting styles in a registry gets awkward. The registry flushes when the shell is ready, and a section that arrives later needs its own flush. Here the CSS is part of what a component renders, so it arrives in the same chunk as the markup it styles:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Flex&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@box-kite/react/components/flex&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;H2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;P&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@box-kite/react/components/semantics&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Suspense&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetchTotals&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Promise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;resolve&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setTimeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;resolve&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;700&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;revenue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;€48,200&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;orders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1204&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Totals&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;totals&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetchTotals&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Flex&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"column"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;gap&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;6&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;borderRadius&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;b&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;borderColor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"emerald-500"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;H2&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;fontSize&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;18&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;fontWeight&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;600&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;totals&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;revenue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;H2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;P&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;fontSize&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;14&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;color&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"slate-600"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        from &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;totals&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;orders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; orders this month
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;P&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Flex&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Dashboard&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Suspense&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;fallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;P&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;color&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"slate-500"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Loading totals…&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;P&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Totals&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Suspense&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The example app in the repository has a section like this behind a 700 ms wait. Its smoke test checks the served HTML: the fallback, the late markup and the late section's own rule are all in the response. A style element that arrives after the shell is streamed disabled (&lt;code&gt;media="not all"&lt;/code&gt;), and React turns it on when it reveals the boundary, so the late section never shows unstyled.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Themes without a provider
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A provider can't run on the server, but a theme doesn't need one. In Box Kite a theme rule is scoped to an ancestor carrying the theme's class. The server decides the theme by putting that class on &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ReactNode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;RootLayout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ReactNode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;lang&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"en"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"dark"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;data-theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"dark"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Every &lt;code&gt;theme={{ dark: … }}&lt;/code&gt; below it applies from the first paint. Switching later means changing that one class in the browser, which re-renders nothing. &lt;a href="https://www.box-kite.dev/blog/dark-mode-without-the-flash" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Dark mode without the flash&lt;/a&gt; covers the rest: the reader's own preference, a stored choice, and the few lines that run before the first paint.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Client components: one line, once
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Most apps still have interactive parts. A client component resolves the &lt;em&gt;client&lt;/em&gt; build of Box, which by default writes its rules through the CSSOM after hydration. That works, but it means the server-rendered HTML of an island would arrive without its CSS. One module puts the island on the same path as the server:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;use client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Box&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@box-kite/react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Box&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;configure&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;sink&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;element&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Import it from your client components, and an island's rules are in the HTML before it hydrates, under the same class names the server used.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The ready-made components split the same way. &lt;code&gt;Flex&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Grid&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Button&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Textbox&lt;/code&gt;, the headings and the other semantic elements, the SVG elements and &lt;code&gt;Icon&lt;/code&gt; call no hook, so a Server Component renders them with their CSS. Those that hold state, such as &lt;code&gt;Dialog&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Menu&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Tabs&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;DataGrid&lt;/code&gt;, ship with a &lt;code&gt;'use client'&lt;/code&gt; banner. Importing one into a Server Component opens a client boundary rather than failing the build.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The honest limits
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;It is runtime CSS-in-JS on the server.&lt;/strong&gt; About 11 µs per Box in the measurement above. That's small next to a database call, but it isn't zero, and a page of thousands of different elements will notice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The CSS isn't a cached file.&lt;/strong&gt; It travels with every HTML response: about 9 KB more than a CSS module at 1,000 cards, gzipped, and the base stylesheet on every page.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;React 19 only.&lt;/strong&gt; Hoisting &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;style href precedence&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; arrived in React 19. On React 18, keep the default mode, which writes to a stylesheet from the client.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;Box.Theme&lt;/code&gt; and hover-callback children stay on the client.&lt;/strong&gt; They need state. The theme &lt;em&gt;rules&lt;/em&gt; work on the server, as shown above.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Your own CSS wins.&lt;/strong&gt; Every Box rule sits in a cascade layer, so an unlayered stylesheet of yours overrides it. That's usually what you want, but it surprises people who expect props to win.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Try it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://www.box-kite.dev/server-components" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React Server Components&lt;/a&gt; is the reference for this mode, including server rendering without Server Components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;examples/next-app&lt;/code&gt; in the &lt;a href="https://github.com/box-kite/box-kite" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;repository&lt;/a&gt; is the App Router app the checks above run against: a streamed section, a client island, a theme toggle and a page of the ready-made components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;npm install @box-kite/react&lt;/code&gt;, then import &lt;code&gt;Flex&lt;/code&gt; into a page that has no &lt;code&gt;'use client'&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally published on &lt;a href="https://www.box-kite.dev/blog/styling-server-components/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;box-kite.dev&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt; Box Kite is open source under MIT — if it is useful to you, a star on &lt;a href="https://github.com/box-kite/box-kite" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;GitHub&lt;/a&gt; helps other people find it. Install it with &lt;code&gt;npm install @box-kite/react&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A dark mode should paint the reader's theme on the first frame, switch without re-rendering the page, and let one section disagree with the rest. Most manage one or two of those three jobs. This article builds all three with Box Kite, shows what each line costs, and is explicit about the one piece the library leaves to you.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The examples here are screenshots; they run live in &lt;a href="https://www.box-kite.dev/blog/dark-mode-without-the-flash/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;the original article&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The problem
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Somebody opens your server-rendered page at night with their system set to dark. The HTML arrives, the browser paints it — white — and a moment later JavaScript runs, reads the preference and repaints everything dark. That flash is the most-reported dark-mode bug there is: the &lt;a href="https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/53063" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;long-running Next.js discussion&lt;/a&gt; on it has dozens of replies, and &lt;a href="https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/64391" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;a newer one&lt;/a&gt; opened because the usual fixes broke in the App Router.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The fixes people reach for each trade one problem for another:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Keep the theme in React state&lt;/strong&gt; and pass it to every component. The server cannot know the reader's preference, so it renders a guess; the client renders the truth; React reports a hydration mismatch and the page flashes anyway. Every switch re-renders the tree.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Two sets of CSS variables&lt;/strong&gt;, swapped by a class. This is the right mechanism, but it means a stylesheet of tokens maintained apart from the components that use them, and every new colour is an edit in two places.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Hide the page until JavaScript has decided.&lt;/strong&gt; No flash, and no content either, for as long as the bundle takes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The model: a theme is a class on an ancestor
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In Box Kite a theme is a prop on the element it styles:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Box&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@box-kite/react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Box&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;6&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;borderRadius&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;b&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;bgColor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"white"&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;color&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"slate-900"&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;borderColor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"slate-200"&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;dark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;bgColor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;slate-900&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;color&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;slate-100&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;borderColor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;slate-800&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      The light colours are plain props, the dark ones are in theme.
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Box&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Faa9b2z1sfwey5l4u0y40.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Faa9b2z1sfwey5l4u0y40.png" alt="The same card twice: under a light ancestor and under a dark one." width="800" height="327"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The library turns &lt;code&gt;theme={{ dark: … }}&lt;/code&gt; into an ordinary CSS rule that applies when an ancestor carries the class &lt;code&gt;dark&lt;/code&gt;. Nothing about it happens in React: there is no context to read and no prop to thread through. Which theme is showing is decided by one class on one element — usually &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; — and everything below follows it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That one decision is what makes the other three jobs cheap.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Deciding the theme: &lt;code&gt;Box.Theme&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Box.Theme&lt;/code&gt; is the part that decides. Put it around the app once:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Box&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@box-kite/react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;StrictMode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;createRoot&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;react-dom/client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;App&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;./App&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;createRoot&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;document&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getElementById&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;root&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;render&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;StrictMode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Box&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Theme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;use&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"global"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;storageKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"theme"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;App&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Box&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;StrictMode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;use="global"&lt;/code&gt; writes the theme onto &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. With no choice stored, it follows &lt;code&gt;prefers-color-scheme&lt;/code&gt; — and keeps following it, so a system that switches to dark at sunset takes the page with it. &lt;code&gt;storageKey&lt;/code&gt; persists an explicit choice in &lt;code&gt;localStorage&lt;/code&gt;, and a stored choice wins over the system from then on. A switch is a hook:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Box&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@box-kite/react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@box-kite/react/components/button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;ThemeSwitch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setTheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Box&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useTheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setTheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;dark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;light&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;dark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;props&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;aria-label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Switch theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;dark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Light&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Dark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;setTheme(null)&lt;/code&gt; forgets the stored choice and hands control back to the system.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What a switch costs.&lt;/strong&gt; We measured it in Chrome with a render counter on every component: pressing the switch changed one class on &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;; the component that called &lt;code&gt;useTheme()&lt;/code&gt; re-rendered, because it reads the theme; the page component, whose every colour changed, rendered exactly once in total — on mount. The colours change because the browser re-matches CSS, not because React re-rendered anything.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The first frame: a few lines you own
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Box.Theme&lt;/code&gt; reads the system preference and the stored choice in the browser, after React starts. In a single-page app that is before anything is painted, so there is nothing to flash. A &lt;strong&gt;server-rendered or prerendered&lt;/strong&gt; page is different: the HTML paints before any JavaScript runs, so the theme class has to be on &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; before that first paint — and only a script in the &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;head&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; runs early enough.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The library does not inject one for you; it is yours, and it is short. Ship the light theme in the HTML, and swap it before the body is painted:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight html"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;html&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;lang=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"en"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;class=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"light"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;data-theme=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"light"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;head&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;script&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="kd"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;localStorage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getItem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;matchMedia&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;(prefers-color-scheme: dark)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;matches&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;dark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;light&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="kd"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;root&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;document&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;documentElement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="nx"&gt;root&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;classList&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;remove&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;light&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;dark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="nx"&gt;root&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;classList&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;add&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="nx"&gt;root&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setAttribute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;data-theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;catch &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/script&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/head&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/html&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The key is the same &lt;code&gt;storageKey&lt;/code&gt; the provider uses, and the rule is the same — stored choice first, system second — so when React starts, &lt;code&gt;Box.Theme&lt;/code&gt; resolves the theme the script already chose and leaves &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; alone. We checked that too: with the system set to dark, the class on &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; changed exactly once, from the shipped &lt;code&gt;light&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;dark&lt;/code&gt;, before React ran, and never again; with &lt;code&gt;light&lt;/code&gt; stored, the same page under a dark system kept &lt;code&gt;light&lt;/code&gt; throughout. The &lt;code&gt;try&lt;/code&gt; is for the reader whose browser blocks storage — they get the light theme the HTML shipped, which is also what a reader with JavaScript turned off sees.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Two variations:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;If your server already knows the choice&lt;/strong&gt; — from a cookie, say — render the class on &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; on the server and skip the script. The repository's Next.js example renders &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html className="dark" data-theme="dark"&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; in a Server Component, and the theme needs no provider at all there, because the rules only care about the class.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;If React renders the &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; element&lt;/strong&gt; (Next.js and other frameworks do), the script changes an attribute React also rendered, so add &lt;code&gt;suppressHydrationWarning&lt;/code&gt; to that element — the warning is about exactly the change you meant to make.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is how &lt;a href="https://www.box-kite.dev" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;box-kite.dev&lt;/a&gt; itself works: every page is prerendered in the light theme, and an inline script in the shell switches it before the first paint.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  A section that stays light
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Real pages have parts that ignore the page's theme: a code sample that is always dark, a print preview that is always light, a marketing block with its own colours. Because a theme is a class on an ancestor, a nested &lt;code&gt;Box.Theme&lt;/code&gt; is simply a nearer ancestor:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Box&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@box-kite/react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;PrintPreview&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Box&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Theme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;use&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"local"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"light"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Box&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;6&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;bgColor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"white"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;color&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"slate-900"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;dark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;bgColor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;slate-900&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;color&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;slate-100&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        Light, whatever the page around it is doing.
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Box&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Box&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fhvd5pocn9o0q7i8nswvr.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fhvd5pocn9o0q7i8nswvr.png" alt="The theme switch, the card, and the print preview. With the page dark, the card follows it and the preview stays light." width="800" height="327"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The nested theme is a real boundary, not a second class competing with the first. Each theme rule is written with CSS &lt;code&gt;@scope&lt;/code&gt;, from the theme's class down to the next element that declares a theme of its own, so the dark page's rules stop at the light section's edge — including for a property the inner section never mentions. In the measurement above, the light section kept its light background while the page around it was dark, and kept it through every switch.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The switch, animated
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A theme change can cross-fade the whole page instead of snapping:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Box&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@box-kite/react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ReactNode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Root&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ReactNode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Box&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Theme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;use&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"global"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;storageKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"theme"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;viewTransition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Box&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;viewTransition&lt;/code&gt; runs the switch inside the browser's View Transitions API. Writing it by hand has a trap — the browser captures the page the moment your callback returns, before React has rendered the new state, so a hand-rolled version captures the old theme twice and nothing appears to animate — and the prop flushes the update inside the callback for you. A reader who asked for reduced motion gets the theme change without the cross-fade, and a browser without view transitions simply switches.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Charts follow too
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The theme reaches markup the library did not render, through CSS variables. A chart library takes a colour string; give it a variable, and declare the variable per theme on a container:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ChartContainer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@box-kite/react/components/chart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Line&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;LineChart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ResponsiveContainer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;recharts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;months&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;month&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Jan&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;revenue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;12&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;month&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Feb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;revenue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;18&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;month&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Mar&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;revenue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;15&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;];&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Revenue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ChartContainer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;series&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;revenue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;height&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;60&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ResponsiveContainer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;width&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"100%"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;height&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"100%"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;LineChart&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;months&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Line&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;dataKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"revenue"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;stroke&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"var(--color-revenue)"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;strokeWidth&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;dot&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;LineChart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ResponsiveContainer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ChartContainer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fadkv1o3inhvas3hk2oqs.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fadkv1o3inhvas3hk2oqs.png" alt="The revenue line, in the colour the container declares for the page's theme." width="800" height="327"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;ChartContainer&lt;/code&gt; declares one &lt;code&gt;--color-&amp;lt;series&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; per name, with a value for each theme, so the chart names no colour at all and its dark mode is the page's. The &lt;a href="https://www.box-kite.dev/charts" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;charts page&lt;/a&gt; shows a full example with a grid and axis labels.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The honest limits
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The pre-paint script is yours.&lt;/strong&gt; For a server-rendered page, nothing in the library can run before the first paint; the few lines above are the whole of it, and they have to agree with the &lt;code&gt;storageKey&lt;/code&gt; you gave &lt;code&gt;Box.Theme&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Theme rules need &lt;code&gt;@scope&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Chrome 118, Safari 17.4, Firefox 128 and later. In an older browser the theme rules are dropped — which is why the examples here write the light colours as plain props and only the dark ones in &lt;code&gt;theme&lt;/code&gt;: an old browser then shows a working light page rather than an unstyled one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The system preference only knows light and dark.&lt;/strong&gt; A theme is any class name — &lt;code&gt;high-contrast&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;sepia&lt;/code&gt;, a brand theme — and &lt;code&gt;theme={{ 'high-contrast': … }}&lt;/code&gt; works the same way, but choosing one of those is always an explicit &lt;code&gt;setTheme&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Try it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://www.box-kite.dev/theme-setup" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Theme setup&lt;/a&gt; — the reference for &lt;code&gt;theme&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Box.Theme&lt;/code&gt; and component themes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://www.box-kite.dev/playground" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;The playground&lt;/a&gt; — write a &lt;code&gt;theme&lt;/code&gt; prop and see the rule it produces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;npm install @box-kite/react&lt;/code&gt;, and wrap your app in &lt;code&gt;Box.Theme&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally published on &lt;a href="https://www.box-kite.dev/blog/dark-mode-without-the-flash/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;box-kite.dev&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt; Box Kite is open source under MIT — if it is useful to you, a star on &lt;a href="https://github.com/box-kite/box-kite" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;GitHub&lt;/a&gt; helps other people find it. Install it with &lt;code&gt;npm install @box-kite/react&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Most UI kits try hard to look neutral. &lt;a href="https://plopui.com" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;PlopUI&lt;/a&gt; goes the other way: wobbly sticker buttons, washi-tape tags, a hand-lettered marker font, colors picked by instinct. The whole thing looks like it was drawn on the back of a receipt.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It has one rule: break the visual rulebook, never the accessibility one.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F56jnod82en6rg2p8ecdq.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F56jnod82en6rg2p8ecdq.png" alt="The PlopUI home page: a hand-drawn headline, sticker buttons and doodled characters on paper" width="800" height="478"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The drawing sits on top, never instead
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A PlopUI button is a real &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;button&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. A checkbox is a real checkbox. The hand-drawn outlines, shadows and doodles are decoration layered over native elements, so the browser and screen readers still know exactly what everything is.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That means the boring stuff just works:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tab, Enter and Space do what you expect. &lt;code&gt;Select&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;Menu&lt;/code&gt; also handle arrow keys, Home, End, type-to-jump and Escape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Every interactive component has a keyboard test, and the docs site runs end-to-end tests in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Status never relies on color alone. The error character (Bix) winces and sweats, so the meaning reads even if you can't tell red from green.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Crooked, but the same crooked everywhere
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The hardest part of a "random" look is server rendering. If a button's tilt comes from &lt;code&gt;Math.random()&lt;/code&gt;, the server draws one angle and the browser draws another. React complains about a hydration mismatch, and the button visibly jumps.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So nothing in PlopUI calls &lt;code&gt;Math.random()&lt;/code&gt; while rendering. Every tilt, wobble and jitter comes from a seed:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// hashString is FNV-1a: it turns a string like "Post sketch" into a 32-bit number.&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/** A deterministic random generator: same seed, same sequence, values in [0, 1). */&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;typeof&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;hashString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// mulberry32&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mh"&gt;0x6d2b79f5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;imul&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;^&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;15&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;^=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;imul&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;^&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;7&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;61&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;^&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;14&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;4294967296&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/** A value in [-range, range], rounded so it serializes identically on server and client. */&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;seededTilt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;range&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;2.5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;n&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)();&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;round&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;n&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;range&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;100&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;100&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Same seed in, same crooked line out, on the server and in the browser. The rounding matters too: two decimals means the number is written identically in the server HTML and in React's props.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Built for the App Router
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The package never imports &lt;code&gt;next/*&lt;/code&gt;, so it works in any React 19 app. In Next.js, every interactive component already carries &lt;code&gt;"use client"&lt;/code&gt;, and the static ones (a timeline, a plain tag) stay Server Components and ship no client JavaScript.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It's also light where it counts: everything is tree-shakeable, and a plain &lt;code&gt;Button&lt;/code&gt; is about 5.6 kB gzipped.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The wobble knows when to chill
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every animation respects &lt;code&gt;prefers-reduced-motion&lt;/code&gt;. Turn it on and the motion stops, while state changes still show, just instantly. Looping scenes pause while they're off screen, which took the docs site's idle CPU on a throttled phone from 12% to 0%. And the animated footer has a pause button, because anything that moves for more than five seconds should.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Three packages
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;@plop-ui/react&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: the components, hooks and characters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;@plop-ui/tokens&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: colors with measured contrast, type, motion and five paper surfaces as CSS variables. There's also a &lt;code&gt;tokens.json&lt;/code&gt; for Figma (Tokens Studio).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;@plop-ui/fonts&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Sketchpop, the marker font, under the SIL Open Font License. Every letter is drawn three times and rotates through &lt;code&gt;calt&lt;/code&gt;, so a word like "Shipped!" never repeats the same p twice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Try it
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npm i @plop-ui/react @plop-ui/fonts
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@plop-ui/fonts/fonts.css&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@plop-ui/react/styles.css&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;PlopProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;toast&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@plop-ui/react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;App&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;PlopProvider&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;surface&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"poster"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;buddy&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;toast&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;success&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Sketch posted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;buddy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        Post sketch
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;PlopProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Or skip the install and play with it first: the &lt;a href="https://plopui.com/playground" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Playground&lt;/a&gt; lets you stick components onto paper and copy the code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What it's for
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Creative tools, learning apps, games, portfolios, side projects: anything that should feel made by a person. It's not the right pick for a dense enterprise dashboard where every pixel has to stay quiet.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;PlopUI is free and MIT-licensed: &lt;a href="https://plopui.com" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;plopui.com&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://github.com/Snorlark/plop-ui" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;GitHub&lt;/a&gt;. Issues and pull requests are welcome, and a few are labeled "good first issue". If something breaks, tell me. I'll fix it and thank you by name.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The first time we shipped an agent-written settings panel straight to &lt;code&gt;main&lt;/code&gt;, it looked fine in staging. Then support got three tickets in an hour: a toggle that did nothing for free plans, a “Save” that double-fired on slow networks, and a new empty state that hid the only CTA half our users needed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;CI was green. Visuals looked close. The bug was product judgment the model never had — and we gave 100% of traffic that judgment on day one.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So we stopped treating “agent UI merged” as “agent UI live.” Feature flags became the default release valve for anything an agent touched in the UI layer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The failure mode: merge = rollout
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Agent PRs tempt you to skip the usual caution:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diff is “just UI”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Screenshots look right&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Playwright clicked through the happy path&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reviewer approved the code shape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;None of that answers: does this layout work for the cohort that never sees premium fields? Does the new empty state break the onboarding funnel? Does the regenerated form still respect the old keyboard path power users rely on?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Those are traffic questions. Feature flags are how you ask them without a full revert.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What I flag (and what I don’t)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I flag &lt;strong&gt;user-visible surfaces the agent authored or heavily rewrote&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New panels, modals, empty / error / loading states&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regenerated forms and settings sections&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agent-refactored navigation / IA changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Copy-heavy UI where tone or CTA placement shifted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I usually &lt;strong&gt;don’t&lt;/strong&gt; flag:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pure token / lint / type cleanup with no layout change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test-only or Storybook-only diffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Internal admin tools with a tiny known audience (still stage them; just don’t burn a flag name)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rule of thumb: if a stranger on the free plan could hit it tomorrow, it gets a flag.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The default pattern we use
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Keep it boring. One boolean (or percentage) per agent UI surface, named after the ticket, not the model:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// flags.ts — names are product, not “gpt-panel-v3”&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;flags&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;settingsBillingV2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;booleanFlag&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;settings-billing-v2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;emptyProjectsAgentCopy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;booleanFlag&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;empty-projects-agent-copy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;as const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;In the route / component:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;SettingsBilling&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;enabled&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useFlag&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;settings-billing-v2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;enabled&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;SettingsBillingLegacy&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;SettingsBillingV2&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// agent-authored surface&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Kill switch lives next to the flag definition, not in a Slack thread:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ops: set settings-billing-v2 = false → instant revert without redeploy&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;If your stack is LaunchDarkly / Unleash / Statsig / a homegrown &lt;code&gt;%&lt;/code&gt; cookie — same idea. The important part is &lt;strong&gt;default off for agent UI&lt;/strong&gt;, not which vendor.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Rollout ladder (what we actually do)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Internal / dogfood&lt;/strong&gt; — flag on for the team only. Click the weird paths humans use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;1–5%&lt;/strong&gt; — watch error rate, rage clicks, support tags for that surface.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;25% → 50%&lt;/strong&gt; — only if step 2 is quiet for a real workday, not twenty quiet minutes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;100%&lt;/strong&gt; — then delete the legacy branch when you’re sure, not “someday.”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Agent UI fails differently than human UI: it often fails &lt;em&gt;narrowly&lt;/em&gt; (one plan tier, one locale, one empty-state branch). Small percentages catch that before it becomes a Monday war room.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What I put in the agent prompt
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Feature flags are a release policy. The agent still needs to &lt;em&gt;build&lt;/em&gt; behind them:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Implement this UI behind flag &lt;code&gt;settings-billing-v2&lt;/code&gt; (default off).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Keep &lt;code&gt;SettingsBillingLegacy&lt;/code&gt; working and unchanged.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Do not delete legacy routes/components in this PR.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Wire the flag at the route/section boundary, not inside every leaf.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Add a short “flag off = legacy” note in the PR body.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Without that, agents “helpfully” delete the old panel and leave you with a binary deploy rollback.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  PR template checkboxes
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight markdown"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="gu"&gt;### Agent UI rollout&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; [ ] New/changed user-visible UI is behind a named flag (default off)
&lt;span class="p"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; [ ] Legacy path still renders when flag is off
&lt;span class="p"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; [ ] Flag name matches the ticket / surface (not the model name)
&lt;span class="p"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; [ ] Rollout plan noted: dogfood → % → 100% (or “internal-only”)
&lt;span class="p"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; [ ] Kill switch owner named (who can flip it in prod)
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Reviewers stop arguing “is this ready?” and start asking “who turns it on?”&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Metrics I watch for the first day
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not vanity:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Error / exception rate on the flagged route&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support tickets tagged with that surface&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Funnel drop at the new empty / CTA step&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accessibility smoke (keyboard + one screen reader pass on dogfood)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If any of those spike at 5%, you don’t “monitor overnight.” You flip the flag off and open a fix PR.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Review comments I leave
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When the agent rewrote a panel with no flag:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This surface ships to every user on merge. Wrap it in &lt;code&gt;settings-billing-v2&lt;/code&gt; (default off) and keep legacy until we ramp. Agent UI doesn’t get a free pass on rollout.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When they deleted legacy in the same PR:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Don’t delete &lt;code&gt;SettingsBillingLegacy&lt;/code&gt; here. Flag-off must still work. Removal is a follow-up after 100% + quiet metrics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When the flag is hardcoded &lt;code&gt;true&lt;/code&gt; “for testing”:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hardcoded &lt;code&gt;true&lt;/code&gt; is a silent 100% rollout. Use the real flag client; leave default false in prod config.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What I stopped doing
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Merging agent UI straight to 100% because staging looked pretty&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Naming flags after models (&lt;code&gt;gpt-settings-rewrite&lt;/code&gt;) instead of product surfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Letting the agent delete legacy in the same PR that introduces the new UI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treating “Playwright green” as “safe for everyone”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Feature-flagging AI-suggested UI isn’t distrust of the model — it’s admitting the model never saw your free-plan edge cases, your support queue, or your Monday traffic. Ship the code when it’s ready. Ship the &lt;em&gt;exposure&lt;/em&gt; when the numbers say so.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Flrpozas9atdwgpqals3y.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Flrpozas9atdwgpqals3y.png" alt="OrderCraft Terminal" width="800" height="469"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Modern financial charting platforms have converged on the same frustrating cloud SaaS model: lock basic technical analysis behind $15 to $60/month subscriptions, restrict free users to 2 indicators per chart, paywall multi-chart split-screen layouts, and force all your watchlists and layouts into their cloud.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On the flip side, developers who try to build hosted open-source alternatives hit two massive walls almost immediately:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;IP Rate Limits:&lt;/strong&gt; Public exchange APIs (like Binance or Yahoo Finance) ban central server IPs within hours when multiple users request market data through a shared backend.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Market Data Redistribution Licensing:&lt;/strong&gt; Exchanges demand thousands of dollars per month the moment a central server redistributes market feeds to third-party users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To solve both problems at the root, I built and open-sourced &lt;strong&gt;OrderCraft&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;v0.1.0&lt;/code&gt;, MIT License) — a high-performance, &lt;strong&gt;100% local-first&lt;/strong&gt; financial charting and technical analysis terminal built with &lt;strong&gt;Go&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;React 19&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;TypeScript&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;Lightweight Charts&lt;/strong&gt; (Apache-2.0).&lt;/p&gt;


